{"name":"Fermata","hex":"#7b7054","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fermata","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The holding of a note or rest for longer than its usual duration.","The notation ⟨◌͒⟩ of such a prolongation, usually represented as a dot with a semi-circle above or below it, written above or below the prolonged note or rest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fermata"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fermata","blocks":[{"text":"A fermata is a symbol of musical notation indicating that the note should be prolonged beyond the normal duration its note value would indicate. Exactly how much longer it is held is up to the discretion of the performer or conductor, but twice as long is common. It is usually printed above but can be occasionally below the note to be extended."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Urlinie_in_G_with_fermata.png/330px-Urlinie_in_G_with_fermata.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fermata"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Beethoven_-_Concerto_in_C_minor%2C_cadenza.png/500px-Beethoven_-_Concerto_in_C_minor%2C_cadenza.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Beethoven_-_Concerto_in_C_minor%2C_cadenza.png/500px-Beethoven_-_Concerto_in_C_minor%2C_cadenza.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cadenza indication from Beethoven's Piano Concerto in C minor: fermata over rest indicates beginning, fermata over shake (trill) indicates close.[1] Playⓘ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeethoven_-_Concerto_in_C_minor%2C_cadenza.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Schubert_-_D._759%2C_I_mm.60-4_G.P..png/500px-Schubert_-_D._759%2C_I_mm.60-4_G.P..png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Schubert_-_D._759%2C_I_mm.60-4_G.P..png/1280px-Schubert_-_D._759%2C_I_mm.60-4_G.P..png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Schubert_-_D._759%2C_I_mm.60-4_G.P..png/500px-Schubert_-_D._759%2C_I_mm.60-4_G.P..png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grand pause (Playⓘ) in Franz Schubert's D. 759, I, mm.60-4. (without G.P.: Playⓘ)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchubert_-_D._759%2C_I_mm.60-4_G.P..png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Fermata_triangle.png/60px-Fermata_triangle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Fermata_triangle.png/120px-Fermata_triangle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Fermata_triangle.png/60px-Fermata_triangle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFermata_triangle.png"}],"sounds":{"fermata":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/87/En-us-fermata.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/87/En-us-fermata.ogg/En-us-fermata.ogg.mp3"}]}}}